<title>USA: Cantor Fitzgerald settles fraud suit with CFTC.</title>
<headline>Cantor Fitzgerald settles fraud suit with CFTC.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cantor Fitzgerald &amp; Co, a New York partnership, agreed to pay penalities to settle civil charges they violated federal commodities laws, the Commodity Futures Trading Commission said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cantor, a broker-dealer and futures commission merchant agreed to pay $500,000 in civil penalities for aiding and abeting the fraud and registration violations of First Republic Financial Corp formerly known as Vancorp Financial Services.</p>
</text>
